 ## Known limitations
 
-Access to vector registers and CSRs is currently not supported.
+Access to vector registers is currently not supported.  A versioned
+Sail-specific extension exposes the current privilege and the core machine and
+supervisor trap/control CSRs through `p` and `P` packets.  Clients can detect it
+from `sail-riscv-debug-v1+` in the `qSupported` response and fetch its stable
+register map from `qXfer:features:read:sail-riscv-debug.xml`.
 
+Memory can be written with either the binary `X` packet or the hexadecimal `M`
+packet.
